{
 "netpack": 1,
 "name": "avenue_junctions",
 "version": "0.2.0",
 "author": "netmod (task avx, task avjunc)",
 "description": "Avenue junctions as one paved box (task avx), reworked for one-way avenues (task avjunc, 2026-10-19: 2 lanes each way, right-hand traffic). sc3netmod's AVX block finds every junction on a straight avenue (road x avenue, road T, T's offset by a cell, avenue x avenue, avenue T, an avenue ending on a road), paves it across both halves (the median opening: every turn and U-turn works inside the box) and gives each box cell the lanes of its edges: two lanes in, two out, two-way or closed. Avenue x avenue boxes form a one-way ring. The halves beside a box carry the median nose (one-way, avcore's lanes). An arm whose avenue avcore leaves two-way gets two-way edges. Box cells save as 43 / 39 / 11203 / 29, noses as 11204, so a game without the mod loads stock junctions. Build: `py -3.12 -m netmod.avjunc_build build .` in re/tools (art from the game's frames, not shipped).",
 "game": {
  "Apps/SIMNTWRK.DLL": "693f65724a08f1bbc920c4ede1b6c1d5c78c8b95fce0164da10b03fbfe526f61"
 },
